From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corentin Wallez <cwallez@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:11:30 -0700
Subject: [dawn][vk] Allow querying and filtering on Vulkan device/driver
 UUIDs.

Two new chained structs are added in VulkanBackend.h (because it is not
possible to declare a uint8_t[VK_UUID_SIZE] in dawn.json), with
additions to ChainUtilsImpl and tests.

 - AdapterPropertierVulkanUUIDs returns the device/driver UUIDs when
   chained in an AdapterInfo.
 - RequestAdapterOptionsVulkanUUIDs filters the returned adapters to
   return only the ones with matching device/driver UUIDs.

Other small changes are:

 - ChainUtils.h STypeFor is fixed to support extensions in ChainUtilsImpl
   for out structs.
 - VulkanDeviceInfo member names are aligned to all end with
   "Properties".

Bug: 563358700
Change-Id: I19231b0a77f97e3d62ffcaa6eed32d609c099427
Reviewed-on: https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/347715
Reviewed-by: Loko Kung <lokokung@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Corentin Wallez <cwallez@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y): the Dawn revision on this branch
predates the AdapterBase::ValidateGetInfo() refactor, so the
AdapterPropertiesVulkanUUIDs feature check was added to
AdapterBase::APIGetInfo() using the branch's existing
hadError/ConsumedError pattern instead of DAWN_INVALID_IF in
ValidateGetInfo(); the check itself (requires FeatureName::AdapterPropertiesVk)
is unchanged. In dawn.json the SType values 82-84 (render bundle encoder
resource table, dawn shader source SPIRV, shared buffer memory host pointer
descriptor) do not exist on this branch, so only values 85 and 86 were
added after 81, keeping the upstream numeric values. All other hunks
applied verbatim.

